From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <muthukumardce@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 00:20:53 +0530
Subject: Revert anti-fingerprint TLS + HTTP/2 SETTINGS randomization

These two changes inverted the intended threat model. The "make every
session look unique" jitter produced TLS / HTTP-2 SETTINGS hashes that
match no known stock Chrome build, which is precisely the signal
Akamai / Cloudflare / Datadome use to flag automation. Reverting both
restores Chrome-canonical, deterministic-per-build bytes.

== net/http/http_network_session.cc ==

Remove the jitter block from AddDefaultHttp2Settings():

    http2_settings[spdy::SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE] +=
        static_cast<int32_t>(base::RandGenerator(8192)) - 4096;
    http2_settings[spdy::SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE] +=
        static_cast<int32_t>(base::RandGenerator(131072)) - 65536;
    http2_settings[spdy::SETTINGS_MAX_HEADER_LIST_SIZE] +=
        static_cast<int32_t>(base::RandGenerator(16384)) - 8192;

Observed Falcon emission BEFORE this revert (via tls.peet.ws):

    1:62528;2:0;4:6246171;6:262579|15663105|0|m,a,s,p
    akamai_fingerprint_hash = 0cad8318a3b8e1f99cfbdf9846b5cff2

All three numeric SETTINGS were off by a random delta within the jitter
window (65536-3008, 6291456-45285, 262144+435), producing a fingerprint
hash that no stock Chrome build emits. Bot managers that fingerprint the
HTTP/2 SETTINGS frame (Akamai notably) get an instant "not real Chrome"
signal on every HTTPS connection before any JS even runs.

Observed Falcon emission AFTER this revert:

    1:65536;2:0;4:6291456;6:262144|15663105|0|m,a,s,p
    akamai_fingerprint_hash = 52d84b11737d980aef856699f885ca86

This is the canonical Chrome 144 hash, matching every stock Chrome
session on every machine.

== net/socket/ssl_client_socket_impl.cc ==

Two changes in SSLClientSocketImpl::Init():

1. Removed Fisher-Yates shuffle of TLS supported_groups + the parallel
   re-sync of key_shares. Restored the original `const` declarations
   in their natural order so the ClientHello sends groups in Chrome's
   fixed canonical order.

2. Removed the random TLS 1.2 cipher-drop block that excluded each of
   {ECDHE_ECDSA_CHACHA20_POLY1305, ECDHE_RSA_CHACHA20_POLY1305,
   ECDHE_ECDSA_AES_256_GCM_SHA384, ECDHE_RSA_AES_256_GCM_SHA384} with
   1/3 probability. The dropped ciphers caused the JA4 cipher count to
   bounce between 11-15 per session, producing JA4 hashes that match
   no published Chrome fingerprint.

Observed JA4 BEFORE this revert (one session sample):

    t13d1416h2_4f2acddecbd5_d8a2da3f94cd   (14 ciphers)

AFTER this revert:

    t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_d8a2da3f94cd   (15 ciphers, every session)

This is Chrome 144's deterministic JA4 for the supported-groups +
cipher-list combination, matching every stock Chrome 144 build.

== Rationale ==

TLS / HTTP-2 SETTINGS fingerprints identify the *browser build*, not
the machine. Same Chrome 144 on Windows / Mac / Linux / different
hardware produces byte-identical hashes. Bot detectors maintain a
database of known-good Chrome hashes and match against them; anything
not in the database is flagged.

Randomizing those bytes per-session does the OPPOSITE of evading
detection - it guarantees we never match. The fingerprint to defeat
isn't "are all sessions from this user identical" (they should be);
it's "does each session match a known stock Chrome build" (it must).

This commit reverts the bytes only. The hunks in the corresponding
Electron-side patch file
(electron/patches/chromium/anti-fingerprint_tls_ja4_randomization_http_2_jitter_cdc_rename.patch)
also need to be removed in a separate commit on that repo so a clean
gclient-sync + apply-all-patches doesn't reintroduce the regression.

Verified by post-rebuild measurement against https://tls.peet.ws/api/all
on FalconBrowser; both JA4 and akamai_fingerprint_hash now match
published Chrome 144 values exactly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/net/http/http_network_session.cc b/net/http/http_network_session.cc
index ce7036ba651cd40b75adcd310772a8eddde5154b..8306a71b26506385faa6543e45aa691eee1cceed 100644
--- a/net/http/http_network_session.cc
+++ b/net/http/http_network_session.cc
@@ -81,14 +81,6 @@ spdy::SettingsMap AddDefaultHttp2Settings(spdy::SettingsMap http2_settings) {
         kSpdyMaxHeaderListSize;
   }
 
-  // Add jitter to HTTP/2 SETTINGS to vary fingerprint per-session.
-  http2_settings[spdy::SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE] +=
-      static_cast<int32_t>(base::RandGenerator(8192)) - 4096;
-  http2_settings[spdy::SETTINGS_INITIAL_WINDOW_SIZE] +=
-      static_cast<int32_t>(base::RandGenerator(131072)) - 65536;
-  http2_settings[spdy::SETTINGS_MAX_HEADER_LIST_SIZE] +=
-      static_cast<int32_t>(base::RandGenerator(16384)) - 8192;
-
   return http2_settings;
 }
 
